<%= @brand.name %> now works with Claude

Hi <%= @user.first_name.presence || 'there' %>,

AI Apps is now turned on for <%= @company.name %>. Your team can connect Claude to <%= @brand.name %> and ask it about leads, deals, inventory, service, the books, budgets, install projects and commission plans, using the same information they already see in <%= @brand.name %>.

1. CHOOSE WHO CAN USE IT
You are an admin, so you already have access. For anyone else, open Settings, Users, Roles & Permissions and give their role the AI Connector permission: Read to connect, Update to let Claude make changes for them.
<%= @roles_url %>

2. INSTALL IT IN CLAUDE
- In Claude, open the directory and add <%= @brand.name %>: <%= @install_url %>
- Sign in with your <%= @brand.name %> login.
- To let Claude make changes, tick "Also let it make changes" on the sign-in screen.

3. THINGS TO ASK
- "Which of my leads are going cold, and what should we do about them?"
- "My bank feed is behind. Help me get it caught up."
- "How are my install projects going this week? Draft the customer updates."
- "I want to rethink how my salespeople get paid. Walk me through it."
- "Help me rough out a budget for next year."
- "Help me close last month."

GOOD TO KNOW
- Claude sees only what each person can see in <%= @brand.name %>, at their locations.
- It asks before every change, and every change is recorded. Review and undo them under Settings, Integrations, AI Apps: <%= @ai_apps_url %>
- It never messages your customers, activates campaigns, workflows, budgets or commission plans, pays bills or deletes records. Those stay in <%= @brand.name %>.
- Dealer cost and gross stay hidden from Claude unless you turn on "Let AI apps see dealer cost and gross" on the same AI Apps page.

More detail: <%= @docs_url %>
Questions? Write to <%= @brand.support_email %>.
